	(text "Radio port (one sheet, used for R1, R2, R3; references 1xx, 2xx, 3xx). Connectors: root sheet.\nK0: coil off = radio on the RX row (fail-safe), coil on = TX row. K0 coil on +12V_RLY (not switched\nby RLY_EN). R1: K0 from PTT in hardware (R51 on the controller); R2, R3: K0 from U903 IO1_3, IO1_4 after the handshake (D-63).\nRow relays: COM on the row bus (L1), NO on the column (L2), NC open. Coils on +12V_SW (switched by RLY_EN).\nCoil drivers: BSS138BK per coil, 100k gate pull-down, 1N4148W to CLAMP_SW (rows) or CLAMP_RLY (K0);\none 24 V zener per clamp net on the power sheet. Qn, Dn, Rn belong to relay Kn. *_DRV are 3.3 V logic inputs.\nEXP: the 5th position of both rows joins on one SMA per radio. The EXP relay is the series disconnect.\nSR-01 (D-103): on a receive-only column (unit 1: A2) the TX relay and its driver are not fitted, in all three radios.\nNo contact exists between a TX row and that column. The firmware keeps a column table (TX or RX only).\nRules (firmware and interlock): max one relay closed per row; TX row never on an RX-only column;\nnothing moves while PTT or RF_DET is active; break before make. Unit 2 build option: not drawn yet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 256.54 0)
